10376	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s2","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s2-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-17T05:55:47.586Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Returning 'none' before any policy has been fetched satisfies the upstream offline rule.","evidence":"DEF ac9 requires that a previously fetched policy be used and 'otherwise the action is refused with the reason'. The LLD explicitly permits a repository with no sighting or fetched policy to return 'none', even when its remote actually carries a policy. Its final open question accepts this exception, but the checked upstream documents do not. This permits unguarded actions in the specified offline case. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md, docs/plans/team-workflow.md]","action":"Obtain an upstream amendment explicitly accepting this bootstrap limitation, or design an initialization requirement that distinguishes verified absence from an unknown policy.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing writeAtomic helper uses a fixed temporary filename and cannot supply the proposed create-only publication semantics.","evidence":"The complete writeAtomic body constructs `const tmp = `${absPath}.tmp``, calls writeFileSync, then renameSync. It neither generates unique temporary names nor uses a no-clobber hard link. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"Keep the proposed unique-temp and create-only publication implementation separate from this helper.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Policy reading, sightings, refresh and team commands are new capabilities.","evidence":"Source searches for TeamPolicy, PolicyReader, PolicyResult, sightings and team command names found no implementations. Reading the workflow gates, tracker helpers, Services composition and command dispatcher confirmed that existing approval and CLI paths do not provide these capabilities. TeamPolicy and PolicyReader currently appear as HLD interface sketches. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts, src/cli/command.ts, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md]","action":"Introduce the policy module and exported contracts explicitly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The listed gates.ts locations are existing TeamPolicy field-add call sites.","evidence":"The cited region implements headFullSha and approveArtifactByJsonPath; it contains `execFileSync('git', ['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], ...)` and approval metadata handling. There is no TeamPolicy declaration or consumer anywhere in the searched source. These locations cannot describe a source.anchorKnown field addition to an existing code type. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md]","action":"Distinguish the HLD contract amendment from the new TypeScript declaration, name its destination, and identify gates.ts as a future s5 consumer rather than an s2 field-add call site.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Services, makeServices, command dispatch and the two handwritten Services test facades are the relevant CLI integration sites.","evidence":"Services declares the facade and makeServices binds implementations. runCommand tokenizes commands and switches on the first token. command.test.ts constructs `const base: Services`; tui.test.ts defines `fakeServices(): Services`. The existing services.test.ts uses makeServices rather than constructing another facade. [files: src/cli/services/index.ts, src/cli/command.ts, src/cli/__tests__/command.test.ts, src/cli/__tests__/tui.test.ts, src/cli/__tests__/services.test.ts]","action":"Add the team facade and dispatch as specified, and verify the real makeServices binding alongside fake-service command tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"An artifact approved between initial policy adoption and policy reintroduction is grandfathered under the HLD.","evidence":"The HLD states: 'an artifact whose approvedAt is earlier than that time is treated as signed off', where that time belongs to the first default-branch commit carrying the policy. An approval between adoption and reintroduction is later than that anchor. The LLD edge-case table nevertheless says such an artifact 'is grandfathered exactly as the HLD states'. Implementing that expectation would bypass required signoff. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/S002/LLD.md]","action":"Correct the edge case and its test expectation: only approvals before the original adoption timestamp are grandfathered; approvals between adoption and reintroduction are not.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Policy loading, caching, anchor discovery and starter setup belong to s2; enforcement and signoff remain other Stories' responsibilities.","evidence":"HLD §5.2 assigns s2 'Reading the policy file from the remote default branch ref, the cached last-fetched copy and the offline rule, finding the first default-branch commit ... the starter policy and the team setup command.' sc4 belongs to s5 and sc5 to s7. The proposed implementation stays within that division and retains the sc2 PolicyResult envelope. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md, src/workflow/amendments/types.ts, src/workflow/amendments/applier.ts]","action":"Keep gate installation and grandfathering decisions in their owning Stories; record anchorKnown through the proposed shared-contract amendment.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Throwing from either asynchronous team service can produce the specified cross-prefixed command-bar error.","evidence":"runCommand wraps dispatch in try/catch and returns `✗ ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`. Its asynchronous branches use `return await`, which catches promise rejection within this boundary. [files: src/cli/command.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts]","action":"Use `return await runTeam(...)` in the new dispatch case and convert PolicyResult failures into Errors in the service wrappers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The policy remote can be resolved unambiguously from the specified contract.","evidence":"The LLD repeatedly uses 'the remote' and stores a remote in PolicySighting, but supplies no initial selection rule for multiple remotes or a repository without origin. Existing tracker target resolution explicitly uses gitOriginOwnerRepo and origin; that resolves a GitHub target, not a policy remote contract. No policy implementation exists to resolve the omission. Analyzer tools were unavailable, so this was checked through source searches and file reads. [files: src/workflow/config/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/S002/LLD.md]","action":"Specify initial remote selection, behavior when it is ambiguous or missing, and whether a sighting's remote remains authoritative after configuration changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The proposed ac9 tests cover the complete upstream acceptance criterion.","evidence":"DEF ac9 requires refusal when the remote is unreachable and no previously fetched policy exists. The LLD maps this to a 'known team repo' test and an explicit refresh failure test, omitting a workflow action in a never-fetched repository with no sighting. Its open question instead specifies 'none' for that case. The proposed tests therefore cannot establish the full criterion. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/S002/LLD.md]","action":"Add the no-sighting/no-fetched-policy offline action case, with its expected result determined by the resolved upstream requirement.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed node:test/tsx approach and the statement that normal compilation excludes test sources match the repository.","evidence":"The existing command and TUI suites import test from node:test and document tsx execution. tsconfig.json excludes `**/__tests__/**` and `**/*.test.ts`. Thus a production build alone will not validate the handwritten test facades. [files: tsconfig.json, src/cli/__tests__/command.test.ts, src/cli/__tests__/tui.test.ts, src/cli/__tests__/services.test.ts]","action":"Run the proposed tests through tsx and include a runtime assertion for the actual team service composition.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":2,"low":7,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-17T05:55:47.586Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
